{"name":"Scarlet Blaze","hex":"#b21f1f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scarlet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brilliant red colour sometimes tinged with orange.","Cloth of a scarlet color."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright red colour.","Sinful or whorish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarlet"},{"term":"blaze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fire, especially a fast-burning fire producing a lot of flames and light.","Intense, direct light accompanied with heat."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be on fire, especially producing bright flames.","To send forth or reflect a bright light; shine like a flame."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blaze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Acacia leprosa","blocks":[{"text":"Acacia leprosa, also known as cinnamon wattle, is a species of flowering plant in the family Fabaceae and is endemic to eastern Australia. It is an erect or spreading, sticky, aromatic shrub, occasionally a tree, elliptic or narrowly elliptic to lance-shaped phyllodes, usually two spherical heads of pale yellow flowers and thinly leathery to firmly papery pods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Acacia_leprosa.jpg/330px-Acacia_leprosa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acacia_leprosa","wikidata":"Q4670955"},{"title":"Acacia leprosa 'Scarlet Blaze'","blocks":[{"text":"Acacia 'Scarlet Blaze' is a cultivar of Acacia leprosa originating from Victoria in Australia. It is noted for its unusual red flowers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Acacia_leprosa_%27Scarlet_Blaze%27_flowers.jpg/330px-Acacia_leprosa_%27Scarlet_Blaze%27_flowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acacia_leprosa_'Scarlet_Blaze'","wikidata":"Q4670950"},{"title":"Scarlet (color